        "id": "15-3-3",
        "topicId": "15-3",
        "topicTitle": "Brand Deals & Sec 194R Tax Rules — Free Products Pe Tax!",
        "cardIndex": 3,
        "totalCardsInTopic": 3,
        "title": "Brand Deals & Sec 194R Tax Rules — Free Products Pe Tax! (Part 3)",
        "content": "3. **Total TDS Credited to Sneha's Form 26AS / AIS**:\n   $$\\text{Total TDS Deposited in Govt Treasury} = ₹10,000 + ₹15,000 = \\text{₹25,000}$$\n\n---\n\n#### Step 2: Calculating Gross Receipts & Filing ITR-4 under Section 44ADA\n\nSneha opts for **Section 44ADA Presumptive Taxation Scheme** for professionals (Ref: **Module 13: Advanced Tax for Freelancers**).\n\n1. **Calculation of Total Gross Receipts**:\n   $$\\text{Gross Receipts} = \\text{Cash Payout Received} + \\text{Fair Market Value of Retained Goods}$$\n   $$\\text{Gross Receipts} = ₹1,00,000 + ₹1,50,000 = \\text{₹2,50,000}$$\n\n2. **Application of Section 44ADA 50% Presumptive Income Rule**:\n   Under Section 44ADA, professionals are presumed to have spent 50% of their gross receipts on business operational expenses without needing to preserve expense bills or bills receipts!\n   $$\\text{Net Taxable Business Income} = 50\\% \\times \\text{Gross Receipts}$$\n   $$\\text{Net Taxable Business Income} = 50\\% \\times ₹2,50,000 = \\text{₹1,25,000}$$\n\n---\n\n#### Step 3: Income Tax Calculation & Rebate under New Tax Regime\n\nLet me compute Sneha's final tax liability under the **New Tax Regime** (FY 2025-26):\n\n```markdown\nSneha's Tax Computation Breakdown:\n- Gross Taxable Income: ₹1,25,000\n- Basic Exemption Limit (New Tax Regime): ₹3,00,000\n- Tax Payable as per Slab Rates: ₹0\n- Tax Rebate under Section 87A (Income < ₹7,00,000): Full Rebate\n- Net Final Tax Payable: ₹0.00\n```\n\n---\n\n#### Step 4: Claiming the 10% TDS Refund from Income Tax Department! 🎉\n\nSneha files her annual tax return **ITR-4 (Sugam)** before July 31st:\n- Calculated Net Tax Liability: **₹0**\n- Total TDS Already Paid & Recorded in Form 26AS: **₹25,000**\n- **NET REFUND DUE TO SNEHA**: **₹25,000 + Statutory Interest @ 0.5% per month!**\n\n> **GOLDEN LESSON**: Thousands of student creators lose their TDS money every year because they think *\"Mujhe tax nahi dena toh ITR file kyun karu?\"* \n> \n> If TDS was deducted from your brand payments or free products, **filing your ITR is the ONLY way to get that 100% money refunded directly into your bank account!** (Ref: **Module 10 & Module 13**).\n\n---",
