        "topicTitle": "Creator Contracts, Licensing & Invoicing",
        "cardIndex": 1,
        "totalCardsInTopic": 3,
        "title": "Creator Contracts, Licensing & Invoicing",
        "content": "Dekho bhai, creator economy mein student creators ke saath hone wala 90% financial fraud aur payment dispute ek hi wajah se hota hai: **\"WhatsApp DM Agreements & Oral Commitments\"**. \n\nPR managers text karte hain: *\"Bhai shoot start kar de, invoice bhej de, payment next week pakka clear ho jayegi!\"* Fast forward 90 days later: PR manager is not answering WhatsApp messages, and the brand is claiming they never authorized the campaign fee!\n\nContracts, licensing agreements, and formal invoices are NOT useless bureaucracy — they are your **LEGAL BULLETPROOF ARMOR**.\n\n---\n\n### 10 Non-Negotiable Contract Clauses Every Creator Must Check\n\nJab bhi koi brand, PR agency, ya corporate client tumhe legal contract (Influencer Service Agreement) send kare, sign karne se pehle in 10 clauses ko **magnifying glass** se read karo:\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                  10 ESSENTIAL CREATOR CONTRACT CLAUSES                   │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 1. Scope of Work (SOW) & Revision Cap                                    │\n│ 2. Usage Rights, Licensing Tenure & Territory                            │\n│ 3. Whitelisting / Spark Ads Access Rights                                │\n│ 4. Exclusivity & Category Non-Compete Scope                              │\n│ 5. Payment Terms & Late Payment Interest Clause                          │\n│ 6. IP Ownership & Raw Asset Rights                                       │\n│ 7. Termination & Kill Fee Clause                                         │\n│ 8. Indemnity & Liability Limit Cap                                       │\n│ 9. Governing Law & Dispute Jurisdiction                                  │\n│ 10. Force Majeure & Campaign Cancellation                                │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n#### Clause 1: Scope of Work (SOW) & Revision Cap\n- **The Risk**: Brands asking for 10 rounds of script rewrites, re-shoots, and endless editing changes after video delivery.\n- **Protective Text**:\n  > *\"Deliverables are strictly limited to: (a) 1x YouTube Video Integration (60-90 seconds), (b) 1x Instagram Reel. The agreed compensation includes up to a maximum of two (2) rounds of minor edits. Any additional revisions, re-shoots, or structural changes requested by the Brand shall be billed separately at ₹5,000 per revised iteration.\"*\n\n#### Clause 2: Usage Rights, Licensing Tenure & Territory\n- **The Risk**: Signing away \"Perpetual & Worldwide Usage Rights\". This allows the brand to put your face on billboard ads, TV commercials, and social media ads FOREVER without paying a single extra rupee!\n- **Protective Text**:\n  > *\"Creator grants the Brand a non-exclusive, limited license to re-share the sponsored content on the Brand's official digital social media handles for a period of ninety (90) days from publication date. Commercial usage on Television, Billboards, Print Media, or OTT Platforms is strictly excluded unless covered under a separate Licensing Fee Agreement.\"*\n\n#### Clause 3: Whitelisting & Spark Ads Access\n- **Whitelisting (Meta/TikTok)**: Brand obtains access to run paid ads using *your* personal Instagram/Facebook profile identity.\n- **The Risk**: Brand runs aggressive, misleading sales ads targeting your followers, burning your personal brand credibility.\n- **Rule**: Never include Whitelisting in your base fee! Charge an extra **25% to 50% Monthly Retainer Premium** for Whitelisting ad access!\n\n#### Clause 4: Exclusivity & Category Non-Compete\n- **The Risk**: A brand pays Meera ₹25,000 for a single Reel, but contract clause states: *\"Creator shall not promote, mention, or collaborate with any Fashion, Lifestyle, Beauty, or Apparel brand for a period of 12 months.\"*\n- **Financial Disaster**: Meera just locked herself out of ₹4,00,000 worth of future fashion deals over a tiny ₹25,000 payment!\n- **Protective Text**:\n  > *\"Exclusivity shall be strictly confined to direct competing brands within the [Specific Product Sub-Category, e.g., Wireless Noise-Cancelling Headphones] for a maximum period of thirty (30) days post publication.\"*\n\n#### Clause 5: Payment Terms & Late Payment Penalty\n- **Industry Standard Payment Cycles**:\n  - **Net 30**: Payment within 30 days of valid invoice submission. (Acceptable).\n  - **Net 60 / Net 90**: Delayed payment cycles. (Charge a 15-20% convenience premium!).\n- **Protective Penalty Clause**:\n  > *\"Payment shall be remitted within 30 days from the invoice date. Any overdue payments past the Due Date shall automatically accrue interest at the rate of 18% per annum (1.5% per month), calculated daily until full settlement.\"*\n\n#### Clause 6: Intellectual Property (IP) & Raw Footage Ownership\n- Raw unedited camera files, project files, and unused footage remain the sole Intellectual Property of the creator. The brand receives only a license to use the final edited video asset.\n\n#### Clause 7: Termination & Kill Fee Clause\n- **The Risk**: You spend 3 days shooting and editing a video, and the brand suddenly cancels the campaign saying \"our marketing strategy changed\".\n- **Protective Text**:\n  > *\"If the Brand terminates this Agreement after script approval or filming commencement for reasons not attributable to Creator's breach, Brand shall pay a non-refundable Kill Fee of 50% of the total agreed contract value if terminated prior to final delivery, and 100% if terminated post final video delivery.\"*\n\n#### Clause 8: Indemnity & Liability Limit Cap\n- Limit your total legal liability to the contract value received so a brand cannot sue a student for millions over a minor error.\n\n#### Clause 9 & 10: Jurisdiction & Force Majeure\n- Ensure legal jurisdiction is in your city/state, and protect against unavoidable delays (platform outages, illness).\n\n---\n\n### Tax Classification: Service Fee vs Intellectual Property (IP) Licensing Fee\n\nTax point of view se, aapke invoice line-items aur SAC Codes par TDS aur GST treatment depend karta hai:",
