        "title": "Creator Contracts, Licensing & Invoicing (Part 3)",
        "content": "Best regards,\nRohan\nRohan Digital Studios\n```\n\n##### Email 2: Firm Escalation & Work Pause Notice (Day T+7)\n```text\nSubject: OVERDUE INVOICE NOTICE: Invoice #RM/2025-26/089 (7 Days Overdue)\n\nDear Accounts Team / [Brand Manager Name],\n\nThis email is to draw your urgent attention to Invoice #RM/2025-26/089 for ₹90,000, which was due on 15 December 2025 and remains unpaid as of today.\n\nAs per our contract terms, please note that we have temporarily paused all ongoing deliverables and whitelisting ad access for active campaigns. \n\nKindly remit the outstanding payment immediately and share the transaction UTR number.\n\nRegards,\nRohan\nRohan Digital Studios\n```\n\n##### Email 3: Pre-Legal Notice under MSMED Act 2006 (Day T+30)\n```text\nSubject: FINAL NOTICE PRIOR TO LEGAL PROCEEDINGS: Invoice #RM/2025-26/089 (Udyam MSME Protection)\n\nTo: Board of Directors / Accounts Head, Nexus Marketing Pvt Ltd\n\nRef: Overdue Invoice #RM/2025-26/089 Amounting to ₹90,000 (30 Days Overdue)\n\nDear Sir/Madam,\n\nDespite repeated reminders dated 10th Dec and 22nd Dec, the payment of ₹90,000 due against services rendered remains unpaid.\n\nPlease be advised that Rohan Digital Studios is a registered Micro Enterprise under the Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises Development (MSMED) Act, 2006 (Udyam Registration: UDYAM-DL-00-1234567).\n\nUnder Section 15 & 16 of the MSMED Act:\n1. Buyers are statutorily mandated to clear payments within 45 days.\n2. Failure to pay within 45 days attracts mandatory compound interest at THREE TIMES (3x) the RBI Bank Rate from the due date.\n\nWe request you to clear the principal amount along with applicable late payment interest within 7 business days, failing which we shall proceed to lodge a legal recovery petition on the MSME Samadhaan Portal (samadhaan.msme.gov.in) without further notice.\n\nSincerely,\nRohan\nSole Proprietor, Rohan Digital Studios\nUdyam Reg: UDYAM-DL-00-1234567\n```\n\n#### The Secret Legal Weapon: MSMED Act 2006 (Udyam MSME Registration)\nIf you register your sole proprietorship / creator business on the Indian Government's **Udyam MSME Portal** (100% free online registration using Aadhaar & PAN - Ref: **Module 13**), Indian law grants you powerful statutory rights:\n\n1. **Section 15 of MSMED Act**: Any buyer who receives goods/services from a registered Micro or Small Enterprise **MUST make payment within 45 days** (if written agreement exists) or **15 days** (if no written agreement exists).\n2. **Section 16 of MSMED Act (Compound Interest Penalty)**: If the client fails to pay within 45 days, by law they are mandated to pay **Compound Interest with Monthly Rests at THREE TIMES (3x) the Bank Rate notified by the Reserve Bank of India (RBI)**!\n3. **MSME Samadhaan Portal (`samadhaan.msme.gov.in`)**: Creators can file an online recovery application directly against defaulting agencies. The Facilitation Council issues legal summons to corporate directors, forcing quick settlements!\n\n---",
